{:edb/db-before-t 1250 :edb/db-after-t 1251 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534563 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:06:55.695Z" 13194139534563 true] [17592186064120 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295661 13194139534563 true] [17592186064282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295626 13194139534563 true] [17592186087659 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295638 13194139534563 true] [17592186092298 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295633 13194139534563 true] [17592186096632 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295668 13194139534563 true] [17592186096737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295654 13194139534563 true] [17592186110500 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295647 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295627 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1089 "q-2355" 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1100 "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by the equation $s(t)={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-15$ where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the velocity after $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1113 #uuid "a35c600c-2a9c-5614-9593-1a6e8005af53" 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1142 true 13194139534563 true] [17592186295626 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =3(3)^{2}-2(3) \\\\  & =27-6 \\\\  & =21\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534563 true] [17592186295627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295628 13194139534563 true] [17592186295627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295629 13194139534563 true] [17592186295627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295630 13194139534563 true] [17592186295627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295631 13194139534563 true] [17592186295627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295632 13194139534563 true] [17592186295627 1040 #